<HEAD><style>.gml-card { --rule: var(--neutral-border-color); --leaf-ink: var(--palette-eucalyptus, var(--palette-2)); --mist-field: var(--palette-mist, var(--palette-4)); }
.photo-reading-panel { background-color: var(--surface-color); border-left: 3pt solid var(--leaf-ink); padding: 22pt 24pt 20pt; box-sizing: border-box; }
.gml-card { background-image: radial-gradient(circle at 22% 18%, color-mix(in srgb, var(--surface-color) 22%, transparent) 0 1pt, transparent 1.4pt); background-size: 15pt 15pt; }
.gml-grid-cell { --cell-radius: 0; }
.botanical-rule { --divider-color: var(--leaf-ink); --divider-thickness: 1pt; }
.botanical-rule.gml-divider { opacity: .72; }
.line-botanical .gml-icon { opacity: .62; }
.care-columns .gml-icon { width: 34pt; height: 34pt; font-size: 24pt; }
.care-list, .comparison-ledger { margin-block-start: var(--heading-gap-above); }
.alt-paths { --marker-font-size: calc(11 * var(--type-anchor, 1pt)); --marker-font-weight: 600; --marker-color: var(--body-color-muted); }
.alt-paths .gml-grid-cell__marker { letter-spacing: .1em; text-transform: uppercase; }
.botanical-badges .gml-icon { width: 58pt; height: 58pt; font-size: 30pt; padding: 11pt; box-sizing: border-box; border: 1pt solid var(--leaf-ink); border-radius: 50%; color: var(--leaf-ink); opacity: .82; }
.ripple-field.gml-grid-cell { background-image: radial-gradient(circle at 70% 56%, transparent 0 18%, color-mix(in srgb, var(--leaf-ink) 45%, transparent) 18.3% 18.7%, transparent 19% 28%, color-mix(in srgb, var(--leaf-ink) 32%, transparent) 28.3% 28.7%, transparent 29%); }
.gml-table { --table-border-color: var(--rule); --table-border-width: 1pt; --table-header-bg: var(--mist-field); --table-header-color: var(--heading-color); --table-header-weight: 600; --table-stripe-bg: color-mix(in srgb, var(--mist-field) 38%, transparent); --table-cell-padding-block: 9pt; --table-cell-padding-inline: 12pt; --table-radius: 0; }
.gml-chart { --gamma-chart-grid-color: var(--neutral-border-color); --gamma-chart-axis-color: var(--body-color-muted); --gamma-chart-text-color: var(--body-color); --gamma-chart-bar-radius: 1pt; }
.gml-card__footer { color: var(--body-color-muted); letter-spacing: .08em; }</style></HEAD>
<section image-layout="blank" id="JREu7msGEz" vertical-align="start" card-margin-hidden="true"><grid direction="vertical" spacing="none"><grid-item id="9Mvt9LbnYo" padding="0" rowspan="42"><grid spacing="none"><grid-item id="vA2gH0uL5i" background-color="palette-1" vertical-align="end" padding="48pt 52pt" colspan="36"><display size="md" font-size="49pt">You don't need a spa.<br>You need a better night.</display></grid-item><grid-item id="V04gS3iWy2" padding="0" colspan="24"><img src="https://cdn-staging.gamma.app/QWjS6fBfpt/generated-images/C2lp3DZ0yu-PRcj0iNHTN.png" saved-media-id="3y8ohc2r8wtquwf" source="image.ai-generated" background="true" image-style="winter-glasshouse" alt="Soft editorial photograph of an empty boutique hotel bedroom prepared for sleep, one low warm bedside lamp, closed blackout curtains, analog alarm clock and a clear uncluttered bedside surface, diffuse blue winter evening light, warm ivory and layered sage-green palette, tactile materials, airy negative space, low contrast, matte finish, no people, no logos, no text" meta="{&quot;width&quot;:1440,&quot;height&quot;:1440}"></grid-item></grid></grid-item><grid-item id="t0aRcNnTtr" background-color="surface" vertical-align="center" padding="30pt 52pt" rowspan="18"><p role="subheading">Stillwater Rooms · a wellness program built for boutique hotels of 20 to 80 keys</p></grid-item></grid></section>
<section image-layout="blank" id="VXvcIkzFZK" vertical-align="start"><grid spacing="none"><grid-item id="CyrlPzKs7u" padding="42pt 52pt 34pt"><p role="eyebrow">The demand signal</p><h1>Your guest checked in already exhausted</h1><grid spacing="small" vertical-sizing="fill"><grid-item id="_Jw62bdfCI" background-color="surface" padding="20pt" colspan="20"><display size="md" font-size="48pt">56%</display><p>cite “rest and recharge” as their number one motivation for leisure travel.</p></grid-item><grid-item id="gXi64GtecR" background-color="palette-4" padding="20pt" colspan="20"><display size="md" font-size="42pt">37% / 36%</display><p>seek nature or better mental health, ahead of sightseeing or nightlife.</p></grid-item><grid-item id="u_GTMT1Xb6" background-color="surface" padding="20pt" colspan="20"><display size="md" font-size="48pt">48%</display><p>intend to add solo days around family travel; more than one in four plan a solo trip.</p></grid-item></grid><p font-size="16pt">The industry calls it <i>hushpitality</i>: quietcations, digital detoxes and luxury defined by what has been removed.</p><p role="caption">The guest who used to ask what is nearby now asks how quiet the room is. · <a href="https://www.ttgasia.com/2026/06/25/the-rise-of-hushpitality/">Source: TTG Asia</a></p></grid-item></grid></section>
<section image-layout="blank" id="YeXZfeNPim" vertical-align="center" card-margin-hidden="true"><grid spacing="none"><grid-item id="NVK-1qovCY" background-color="palette-4" vertical-align="end" padding="44pt 38pt" colspan="24"><p role="eyebrow">Addressable audience</p><display size="xl">100%</display><h3>of occupied rooms</h3><p>No booking, time slot or scheduling friction.</p></grid-item><grid-item id="I2Ab1sSAmh" padding="40pt 52pt 34pt" colspan="36"><h1>Sleep is the only amenity every single guest uses</h1><grid divider="sm neutral-border" vertical-sizing="hug"><grid-item id="J1qpekB-iS" colspan="30"><h2>36%</h2><p>of American adults get insufficient rest.</p></grid-item><grid-item id="EWLu5B5GtV" colspan="30"><h2>$690 billion+</h2><p>sleep-tourism sector, with roughly $400 billion of further growth projected to 2028.</p></grid-item></grid><p>Guests can now judge the levers themselves:</p><labels><label variant="outline">Light</label><label variant="outline">Temperature</label><label variant="outline">Sound</label><label variant="outline">Support</label><label variant="outline">Air</label><label variant="outline">Screens</label></labels><p role="caption"><a href="https://www.hoteltechupdate.com/trends/sleep-tourism-in-2026-what-guests-now-pay-premiums-for">Hotel Tech Update</a> · <a href="https://www.hotel-online.com/index.php/news/travelers-are-booking-vacations-just-to-sleep-better-inside-the-sleep-tourism-boom">Hotel Online</a></p></grid-item></grid></section>
<section image-layout="blank" id="FW7K5lqk6c" vertical-align="start"><grid spacing="none"><grid-item id="DL-v0DKeXa" padding="42pt 52pt 34pt"><h1>The trap is thinking the answer is a spa</h1><grid divider="sm neutral-border" vertical-sizing="fill"><grid-item id="Yi9jwBz6aH" vertical-align="center" colspan="20"><display size="md" font-size="42pt">$111,000</display><h4>per treatment room</h4><p font-size="13pt">Approximate annual upper-upscale benchmark. It works at a scale most boutiques do not have.</p></grid-item><grid-item id="ySzBncA65s" vertical-align="center" colspan="20"><display size="md" font-size="42pt">$18 / $40</display><h4>per occupied room</h4><p font-size="13pt">Average spa revenue in upper-upscale versus luxury properties.</p></grid-item><grid-item id="cdfKhqt_yN" vertical-align="center" colspan="20"><display size="md" font-size="42pt">Payroll</display><h4>is the killer</h4><p font-size="13pt">Major wellness can lift total revenue while its staffing burden continues to weigh on profit.</p></grid-item></grid><hr color="palette-2" thickness="sm" class="botanical-rule"><p font-size="16pt">A 42-key hotel that builds two treatment rooms has bought itself a department, a rota and a licensing problem.</p><p role="caption"><a href="https://www.hvs.com/article/8658-HVS-Performance-Report-Spa-Department-2019">HVS</a> · <a href="https://www.hotstats.com/hotel-industry-resources/minor-wellness-hotels-take-lead-across-2025-performance-metrics">HotStats</a></p></grid-item></grid></section>
<section image-layout="blank" id="qPj3Gleal_" vertical-align="start" card-margin-hidden="true"><grid spacing="none"><grid-item id="b0j9Im4X2M" class="ripple-field" background-color="palette-5" padding="48pt 54pt"><p role="eyebrow">2025 operating signal</p><spacer mode="fill"></spacer><hr color="palette-1" thickness="sm" width="xxs" class="botanical-rule"><display size="lg">In 2025, the small programs started beating the big ones</display></grid-item></grid></section>
<section image-layout="blank" id="djJS1FGEZC" vertical-align="start" card-margin-hidden="true"><grid spacing="none"><grid-item id="4PyJTaAEHI" padding="38pt 48pt 32pt"><h1 font-size="32pt">Minor wellness overtook major wellness on every line that matters</h1><grid spacing="large" vertical-sizing="fill"><grid-item id="VVFA5SAVZM" vertical-align="center" colspan="40"><graph chart-type="bar" show-data-labels="true" y-axis-min="0" color-scheme="theme" gridline-style="solid" chart-font="body" text-size="md" width="560pt" height="285pt"><properties><property key="metric" label="Metric" type="label"></property><property key="minor" label="Minor wellness ($)" type="data"></property><property key="major" label="Major wellness ($)" type="data"></property></properties><data><row><cell>ADR</cell><cell>250</cell><cell>232</cell></row><row><cell>RevPAR</cell><cell>170</cell><cell>161</cell></row><row><cell>GOPPAR</cell><cell>99</cell><cell>89</cell></row></data></graph></grid-item><grid-item id="ayzOp3s7Aw" background-color="surface" vertical-align="center" padding="22pt" colspan="20"><p role="eyebrow">What changed</p><p>ADR: <b>$250 vs $232</b></p><p>RevPAR: <b>$170 vs $161</b></p><p>GOPPAR: <b>$99 vs $89</b></p><p>All three favored smaller programs simultaneously for the first time.</p></grid-item></grid><p role="caption">More than 12,000 properties. A leaner cost base converted revenue to profit more effectively. · <a href="https://www.hotstats.com/hotel-industry-resources/minor-wellness-hotels-take-lead-across-2025-performance-metrics">Source: HotStats</a></p></grid-item></grid></section>
<section image-layout="blank" id="5trRYaAzDt" vertical-align="start"><grid spacing="none"><grid-item id="ypcm2D3uZn" padding="42pt 52pt 34pt"><h1>Curation is the boutique advantage, not a consolation prize</h1><grid divider="sm neutral-border" vertical-sizing="fill"><grid-item id="C-wApj-4UT" vertical-align="center" colspan="20"><display size="md" font-size="38pt">$6.8 trillion</display><p>Wellness economy in 2024, forecast to reach <b>$9.8 trillion by 2029</b>.</p></grid-item><grid-item id="Q1fNo69aX4" vertical-align="center" colspan="20"><display size="md" font-size="38pt">$894 billion</display><p>Wellness-tourism spend in 2024.</p></grid-item><grid-item id="ivLX0I3BPL" vertical-align="center" colspan="20"><display size="md" font-size="38pt">£15–£40</display><p>Potential ancillary revenue per stay from one well-chosen product or experience partnership.</p></grid-item></grid><p font-size="16pt">You are competing with the guest's own bedroom. Product placement, retail and local partnerships are cheaper than resort-scale capacity.</p><p role="caption"><a href="https://globalwellnessinstitute.org/press-room/press-releases/the-global-wellness-economy-hits-a-record-6-8-trillion-and-is-forecast-to-reach-9-8-trillion-by-2029/">Global Wellness Institute</a> · <a href="https://globalwellnessinstitute.org/what-is-wellness/what-is-wellness-tourism/">Wellness tourism data</a> · <a href="https://gobrandmatch.com/resources/ancillary-revenue/boutique-spa-wellness-measurement">BrandMatch</a></p></grid-item></grid></section>
<section image-layout="blank" id="lhZokZJ_m9" vertical-align="start" card-margin-hidden="true"><grid spacing="none"><grid-item id="Z3dKlRfRVQ" background-color="palette-5" padding="48pt 54pt"><p role="eyebrow">The operating model</p><spacer mode="fill"></spacer><hr color="palette-1" thickness="sm" width="xxs" class="botanical-rule"><display size="lg">What Stillwater Rooms installs</display></grid-item></grid></section>
<section image-layout="blank" id="6ozOFbys8H" vertical-align="start"><grid spacing="none"><grid-item id="KLEGByz1UN" padding="42pt 52pt 34pt"><h1>Three layers, none of which is a construction project</h1><grid divider="sm neutral-border" marker="icon" marker-size="large" marker-position="above" vertical-sizing="fill" class="line-botanical care-columns"><grid-item id="RA90OqQitp" vertical-align="center" colspan="20"><grid-item-label><icon src="https://iconscdn.pictographic.ai/image/Hz8dji8ViGQtRpEaaRXyph.svg?stroke=45" source="image.pictographic.icon" alt="hotel room bedside environment" meta="{&quot;description&quot;:&quot;A black shape of a building with a triangular roof, symbolizing accommodation and hospitality, embodying the concept of a hotel.&quot;}"></icon></grid-item-label><h3>The Room</h3><p>A specified sleep environment in every key. The physical product is delivered once.</p></grid-item><grid-item id="S_eY6xj8jA" vertical-align="center" colspan="20"><grid-item-label><icon src="https://iconscdn.pictographic.ai/image/2UpHp5Et1qtd9avl7uJG.svg?stroke=45" source="image.pictographic.icon" alt="weekly calendar recurring sessions" meta="{&quot;description&quot;:&quot;Seven short lines extending from a central point, forming a symmetrical pattern to signify the concept of a week.&quot;}"></icon></grid-item-label><h3>The Rhythm</h3><p>Weekly rituals run by vetted local practitioners on revenue share, not payroll.</p></grid-item><grid-item id="Ry11CGq5g7" vertical-align="center" colspan="20"><grid-item-label><icon src="https://iconscdn.pictographic.ai/image/rtayXmC23ZkFAh5kKFq9.svg?stroke=45" source="image.pictographic.icon" alt="revenue ledger hotel booking" meta="{&quot;description&quot;:&quot;A bar chart icon with increasing bars, symbolizing the concept of revenue, which refers to the total income generated by a business or organization from its sales of goods or services.&quot;}"></icon></grid-item-label><h3>The Ledger</h3><p>Bookable packages loaded into your booking engine so the program appears as revenue.</p></grid-item></grid><hr color="palette-2" thickness="sm" class="botanical-rule"><p font-size="16pt">No treatment rooms. No new department. No licensed-practitioner headcount on your P&amp;L.</p></grid-item></grid></section>
<section image-layout="blank" id="jBhwzthP68" vertical-align="start" card-margin-hidden="true"><grid spacing="none"><grid-item id="SdMdjfYK42" padding="30pt 44pt 26pt"><h1 font-size="32pt">Layer one — the room, specified to six levers</h1><grid marker="icon" marker-size="large" marker-style="solid" marker-shape="circle" marker-position="above" marker-align="start" spacing="small" vertical-sizing="fill"><grid-item id="UBuzdBhyfe" cell-style="subtle" colspan="20"><grid-item-label><icon src="https://iconscdn.pictographic.ai/image/XzTT2wd8WvwZA5HfY8NNuV.svg?stroke=45" source="image.pictographic.icon" alt="blackout curtain bedside lamp"></icon></grid-item-label><h4>Light</h4><p font-size="12pt">Blackout to under 1 lux at the pillow; a 2200K bedside lamp that does not suppress melatonin.</p></grid-item><grid-item id="OUOF2ZCOFO" cell-style="subtle" colspan="20"><grid-item-label><icon src="https://iconscdn.pictographic.ai/image/xqILbkjWNByHuA6d6F6N.svg?stroke=45" source="image.pictographic.icon" alt="quiet room sound waves"></icon></grid-item-label><h4>Sound</h4><p font-size="12pt">Door sweeps and white noise, targeting a measured 30 dBA at the bed.</p></grid-item><grid-item id="_JJNnN0oMN" cell-style="subtle" colspan="20"><grid-item-label><icon src="https://iconscdn.pictographic.ai/image/ftaKq9VUqfQkLeYWRZCa.svg?stroke=45" source="image.pictographic.icon" alt="room thermostat temperature"></icon></grid-item-label><h4>Temperature</h4><p font-size="12pt">18.5°C at turndown; cooling and warming duvet weights offered at booking.</p></grid-item><grid-item id="piqxDrKFBj" cell-style="subtle" colspan="20"><grid-item-label><icon src="https://iconscdn.pictographic.ai/image/Md93iproKhZU2bD3Brq6.svg?stroke=45" source="image.pictographic.icon" alt="mattress pillow support"></icon></grid-item-label><h4>Surface</h4><p font-size="12pt">Mattress topper and three pillow densities, chosen at check-in rather than requested later.</p></grid-item><grid-item id="VMzttc1siD" cell-style="subtle" colspan="20"><grid-item-label><icon src="https://iconscdn.pictographic.ai/image/SH3eo2JYTMy7IbxUkUSD.svg?stroke=45" source="image.pictographic.icon" alt="air purifier filter"></icon></grid-item-label><h4>Air</h4><p font-size="12pt">A quiet HEPA unit per room, with filters on a logged 90-day cycle.</p></grid-item><grid-item id="LIdO1Kj2oM" cell-style="subtle" colspan="20"><grid-item-label><icon src="https://iconscdn.pictographic.ai/image/resPTVcMWK8eITfnQThy.svg?stroke=45" source="image.pictographic.icon" alt="phone charging drawer analog clock"></icon></grid-item-label><h4>Screens</h4><p font-size="12pt">Charging outside arm's reach and an analog alarm clock, so the phone has no excuse.</p></grid-item></grid><p role="caption">Every lever is measurable, so the website promise can be audited.</p></grid-item></grid></section>
<section image-layout="blank" id="R2jXtw7ji9" vertical-align="start" card-margin-hidden="true"><grid spacing="none"><grid-item id="hYWEA15kzA" padding="40pt 50pt 34pt"><h1>Layer two — the rhythm, without the rota</h1><grid spacing="large" vertical-sizing="fill"><grid-item id="CwZuwFHEUk" vertical-align="center" colspan="38"><table col-widths="[20,38,42]" header-row="true" borders="rows" striped="false"><tbody><tr><td><p>Day</p></td><td><p>Session</p></td><td><p>Cadence</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>Tuesday</p></td><td><p>Sunrise breathwork</p></td><td><p>Fixed weekly slot</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>Wednesday</p></td><td><p>Restorative stretch</p></td><td><p>Fixed weekly slot</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>Friday</p></td><td><p>Sunrise breathwork</p></td><td><p>Fixed weekly slot</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>Sunday</p></td><td><p>Sound bath</p></td><td><p>Fixed weekly slot</p></td></tr></tbody></table><p role="caption">Run in space already available: a lobby corner at 7am, a courtyard or a roof terrace.</p></grid-item><grid-item id="AKCdYLuuJ5" background-color="surface" vertical-align="center" padding="22pt" colspan="22"><p role="eyebrow">Operating model</p><p>Stillwater sources, vets, insures and schedules the practitioners.</p><p>They are contracted and paid from session revenue. An empty session costs the hotel nothing.</p><p>The front desk sells it with one line at check-in and a card on the bed.</p><h3>Fixed variable cost: zero.</h3></grid-item></grid></grid-item></grid></section>
<section image-layout="blank" id="CUiFMuNvdg" vertical-align="start"><grid spacing="none"><grid-item id="gxlozPgvlL" padding="38pt 48pt 32pt"><h1>Layer three — the ledger, so it reads as revenue</h1><grid spacing="small" vertical-sizing="fill"><grid-item id="Xc8qUfgNHB" background-color="surface" padding="18pt 20pt" colspan="30"><p role="eyebrow">Rate add-on</p><h3>The Quiet Night package</h3><p font-size="13pt">Full sleep specification, turndown ritual and a late 2pm checkout.</p></grid-item><grid-item id="bKkERKkdZ4" background-color="palette-4" padding="18pt 20pt" colspan="30"><p role="eyebrow">Bookable access</p><h3>Session passes</h3><p font-size="13pt">Single-session drop-in or a stay-length pass, sold at reservation or at the desk.</p></grid-item><grid-item id="pM-3Ny7yMk" background-color="palette-4" padding="18pt 20pt" colspan="30"><p role="eyebrow">Retail margin</p><h3>The takeaway kit</h3><p font-size="13pt">Sleep mask, magnesium balm, caffeine-free tea blend and the room's pillow spray.</p></grid-item><grid-item id="jCrGiY9h82" background-color="surface" padding="18pt 20pt" colspan="30"><p role="eyebrow">Monthly reporting</p><h3>Four operating measures</h3><p font-size="13pt">Attach rate, session fill, retail per occupied room and ADR delta.</p></grid-item></grid><p font-size="15pt">If it is not measured against existing KPIs, it will be cut in the first soft quarter. We measure from week one.</p></grid-item></grid></section>
<section image-layout="blank" id="CUkrvG5aGH" vertical-align="start" card-margin-hidden="true"><grid spacing="none"><grid-item id="pgAScdU99W" padding="26pt 28pt 24pt 40pt" colspan="42"><h1 font-size="30pt">A worked example: The Ardmore, 42 keys</h1><p role="caption"><b>Illustrative example.</b> Stillwater Rooms and The Ardmore are fictional, created for this prototype. The figures below are a transparent model built from the stated assumptions — not results from a real client, and not a forecast of yours.</p><table col-widths="[30,70]" header-row="true" borders="rows" striped="false"><tbody><tr><td><p>Model line</p></td><td><p>Assumption / result</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>Base</p></td><td><p>42 keys · 70% annual occupancy · $265 ADR · 10,731 occupied room-nights</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>Quiet Night package</p></td><td><p>$85 · 12% attach · 1,288 packages · <b>$109,480</b></p></td></tr><tr><td><p>Sessions</p></td><td><p>4/week × 52 · 5 guests × $25 · <b>$26,000</b></p></td></tr><tr><td><p>Retail</p></td><td><p>$3.50 per occupied room-night · <b>$37,559</b></p></td></tr><tr><td><p><b>Gross incremental revenue</b></p></td><td><p><b>$173,039</b></p></td></tr><tr><td><p>Variable costs</p></td><td><p>Practitioner share: 55% of sessions, $14,300 · Retail COGS: 45%, $16,902</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>Program fee</p></td><td><p>$3,200/mo · $38,400</p></td></tr></tbody></table></grid-item><grid-item id="x-X8usgG4a" background-color="palette-4" vertical-align="end" padding="34pt 28pt" colspan="18"><p role="eyebrow">Net contribution</p><display size="md" font-size="48pt">≈ $103,400</display><hr color="palette-2" thickness="sm" class="botanical-rule"><p><b>One-time fit-out:</b> ≈ $26,000</p><p><b>Payback:</b> inside four months</p><p><b>At 8% attach:</b> still clears $65,000</p><p role="caption">The model is yours to stress-test before signing.</p></grid-item></grid></section>
<section image-layout="blank" id="siUw10gMcY" vertical-align="start"><grid spacing="none"><grid-item id="pvB6PSRpJ9" padding="42pt 52pt 34pt"><h1>It should sound like your hotel, not like a franchise</h1><grid spacing="small" vertical-sizing="fill"><grid-item id="KCOGSbTMG-" padding="24pt" border="1.3333333333333333px solid neutral-border" colspan="28"><p role="eyebrow">Chain default</p><h3>Built for replication</h3><p>A corporate team designs one offer to travel across markets. Consistency is the priority.</p></grid-item><grid-item id="Jr3VUYwIsP" background-color="palette-4" padding="24pt" colspan="32"><p role="eyebrow">Boutique advantage</p><h3>Specific to place</h3><p>Local traditions, ingredients and practitioners create differentiation, pricing power and loyalty that commodity wellness cannot.</p></grid-item></grid><grid divider="sm neutral-border" vertical-sizing="hug"><grid-item id="f8nvJzrvEl" colspan="30"><h4>Source locally by default</h4><p font-size="13pt">Tea from a regional producer, balm from a maker within 100 miles, practitioners from your city.</p></grid-item><grid-item id="WoHTno8Gx0" colspan="30"><h4>Write it in your voice</h4><p font-size="13pt">We provide standards. Your team builds the naming, copy and rituals in the onboarding workshop.</p></grid-item></grid><p role="caption"><a href="https://hotelkonzept.com/spa-concept-development-independent-hotels/">Source: Hotel Konzept</a></p></grid-item></grid></section>
<section image-layout="blank" id="0X_FZkkdUh" vertical-align="start"><grid spacing="none"><grid-item id="JF-GIozt3Y" padding="40pt 54pt 34pt"><h1>What it costs and how we get paid</h1><table col-widths="[29,71]" header-row="true" borders="rows" striped="false"><tbody><tr><td><p>Commercial line</p></td><td><p>Terms</p></td></tr><tr><td><h3>$550–$700 per key</h3></td><td><p>Approximate one-time fit-out for the six levers, installed over a low-occupancy week. You own the hardware outright.</p></td></tr><tr><td><h3>Program fee</h3></td><td><p>Flat monthly retainer scaled to key count, covering sourcing, practitioner management, insurance, training, collateral and reporting.</p></td></tr><tr><td><h3>Revenue share</h3></td><td><p>Practitioners are paid from session revenue only, so the share never touches fixed cost.</p></td></tr><tr><td><h3>No lock-in</h3></td><td><p>12-month initial term, then 60 days' notice. The rooms, supplier relationships and training stay with you.</p></td></tr></tbody></table><hr color="palette-2" thickness="sm" width="xs" class="botanical-rule"><p font-size="16pt">We would rather earn the renewal than litigate the exit.</p></grid-item></grid></section>
<section image-layout="blank" id="DcKVhe-hpS" vertical-align="start" card-margin-hidden="true"><grid spacing="none"><grid-item id="AMS9y-CfHt" padding="38pt 46pt 34pt"><h1>Ninety days from signature to first Quiet Night sold</h1><spacer mode="fill"></spacer><grid marker="number" marker-rule="true" marker-position="above" marker-align="start" marker-numbering-format="decimal-leading-zero" spacing="small" vertical-sizing="hug" style="--marker-gap: 0.6em;"><grid-item id="GqgdU2cxTt" colspan="12"><h4>Days 1–14<br>Audit</h4><p font-size="11.5pt">Measure light, sound and temperature in sample rooms. Pull twelve months of ADR and occupancy.</p></grid-item><grid-item id="1D4rh7R4Yo" colspan="12"><h4>Days 15–35<br>Design</h4><p font-size="11.5pt">Workshop with the GM and front-desk lead. Set naming, pricing, suppliers and interviews.</p></grid-item><grid-item id="Kia8Xx07ZN" colspan="12"><h4>Days 36–60<br>Install</h4><p font-size="11.5pt">Fit out floor by floor in the softest week. No room leaves inventory for more than one night.</p></grid-item><grid-item id="Of9hcHpvXz" colspan="12"><h4>Days 61–75<br>Train and load</h4><p font-size="11.5pt">Front-desk scripts, rate plan, photography and a soft launch to repeat guests.</p></grid-item><grid-item id="LfpDU6Sr5-" colspan="12"><h4>Days 76–90<br>Open and measure</h4><p font-size="11.5pt">Full launch, first monthly report and the first attach-rate review against baseline.</p></grid-item></grid><spacer mode="fill"></spacer><p role="caption">The audit sets the baseline. Day 90 tests the offer against it.</p></grid-item></grid></section>
<section image-layout="blank" id="efGW6Z64zv" vertical-align="start" card-margin-hidden="true"><grid spacing="none"><grid-item id="774SpnnYQv" padding="38pt 54pt 30pt"><h1>The four questions every GM asks us</h1><table col-widths="[43,57]" borders="rows" striped="false"><tbody><tr><td><h3>“What if the sessions don't fill?”</h3></td><td><p>They cost nothing when empty. Practitioners are paid from session revenue. We review cadence at day 90 and drop what is not working.</p></td></tr><tr><td><h3>“Will this disrupt housekeeping?”</h3></td><td><p>Turndown adds roughly 90 seconds per room and is trained in one shift. Air filters follow a 90-day log.</p></td></tr><tr><td><h3>“Our rooms are small.”</h3></td><td><p>Every lever is in-room and takes no floor area. Sessions use space you already own and do not currently monetize.</p></td></tr><tr><td><h3>“Can we start with one floor?”</h3></td><td><p>Yes. A 10-key pilot uses the same measurement, then converts to full rollout or ends at 120 days.</p></td></tr></tbody></table></grid-item></grid></section>
<section image-layout="blank" id="5Ggw17YBb1" vertical-align="start" card-margin-hidden="true"><grid direction="vertical" spacing="none"><grid-item id="XOQ6JT6d0T" padding="0" rowspan="12"><img src="https://cdn-staging.gamma.app/QWjS6fBfpt/generated-images/O0wQytE0hZgcMKJpHrPdr.png" saved-media-id="4matx5j9cqa770i" source="image.ai-generated" background="true" image-style="winter-glasshouse" alt="Documentary architectural photograph of a quiet unbranded boutique hotel corridor with a row of ten guest-room doors receding into soft perspective, diffuse winter daylight at the far end, warm ivory walls and muted sage details, clean uncluttered surfaces, low contrast, matte finish, no people, no signage, no logos, no text" meta="{&quot;width&quot;:1920,&quot;height&quot;:1088}"></grid-item><grid-item id="PlMi9EfoDh" vertical-align="end" padding="34pt 54pt 34pt" rowspan="48"><h1>Give us one floor and ninety days</h1><grid divider="sm neutral-border" vertical-sizing="hug"><grid-item id="0SLqfCrZYS" colspan="20"><p role="eyebrow">The ask</p><p>A 10-key pilot, with the audit starting within three weeks.</p></grid-item><grid-item id="xYkhNNOdyA" colspan="20"><p role="eyebrow">You commit</p><p>Fit-out for ten rooms, one workshop morning from your GM and a front-desk briefing.</p></grid-item><grid-item id="QZnaWewnIG" colspan="20"><p role="eyebrow">You get back</p><p>A measured attach rate and a real ADR delta against your own baseline.</p></grid-item></grid><p><b>Walk away at 120 days</b> and keep the rooms, suppliers and data.</p><p font-size="16pt">The guest is already asking for a quieter night. The only question is whether they are paying you for it.</p></grid-item></grid></section>